### [HANDOFF][Termux 0.119.0-beta.3] P0-1 CLOSED — aput-object store-check law `APK_VERIFIED` + W10 boot-advance capability package (3 units)

**Base SHA** `7bbf087a` · **binary sha16** `56cf35bb4f4f3636` · fresh reproduction this session: `/tmp/tdata20` (fresh data root). Local evidence: `docs/evidence/w10_storechk_termux/`, `docs/evidence/w10_selfctx_termux/`, `docs/evidence/w15_bootcl_termux/`. Full patch inline below (recoverable per protocol §8; sandbox may be destroyed).

**Ledger**

| ID | Status | Finding | Patch | Test evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| C6-W10-STORECHK | APK_VERIFIED / INTEGRATION_READY | bogus ArrayStoreException ×17 uncaught @ `ImmutableMap$Builder.put` | view_ancestry.h +3 rows; engine ENTRY law | w10 + fresh tdata20 |
| C6-W10-BOOTCL-V2 | APK_VERIFIED | `HiddenApiBypass.<clinit>` NPE → APP-BOUNDARY process death | view_ancestry.h +4 rows; engine 4 hunks | w15 excerpt |
| C6-W10-SELFCTX | APK_OBSERVED | `createPackageContext(self)` error-dialog path | engine 1 hunk | w10_selfctx excerpt |

---

#### UNIT 1 — [C6-W10-STORECHK] aput-object store-check vs boot-classpath metadata (P0-1)

**A. Finding** — `ImmutableMap$Builder.put` → `aput-object` into `[Ljava/util/Map$Entry;` threw bogus `Ljava/util/AbstractMap$SimpleImmutableEntry; cannot be stored in an array of type [Ljava/util/Map$Entry;` ×17, **all uncaught** → F-016 process-death downgrade; the whole guava `ImmutableMap` construction chain dead.

**B. Root cause** — the store-check itself (R-NEW-010) is correct in shape: it resolves the array's RUNTIME class (`heap_.get_object_class`), strips one bracket pair, and asks `dalvik_class_assignable(src_runtime_class, component)`. The FALSE answer came from **incomplete boot-classpath metadata**: `SimpleImmutableEntry` is a libcore platform class — no APK class_def, no `class_to_interfaces_` DEX-table entry — and `framework_class_interfaces()` had no row for the entry family, so the walk (own interfaces → `framework_implements` → superclass hops) found no `SimpleImmutableEntry → Map$Entry` edge and answered FALSE on a LEGAL store.

**C. Expected** — OpenJDK `java/util/AbstractMap.java`: `SimpleImmutableEntry<K,V> implements Entry<K,V>`; `SimpleEntry<K,V> implements Entry<K,V>, java.io.Serializable`; `AbstractMap<K,V> implements Map<K,V>`. AOSP `art::HandleAPutObject` / `ThrowArrayStoreException`: the check is `Class::IsAssignableFrom(value runtime class, resolved component class)` — a legal store must pass.

**D. Implementation** — `miniandroid/src/framework/view_ancestry.h`, `framework_class_interfaces()` (+21 lines; full diff below). The check itself needs NO change. Companion engine law (same unit): `miniandroid/src/dex/dalvik_engine.cpp`, `bridge_to_api` @34753 — platform `SimpleImmutableEntry/SimpleEntry .<init>(K,V)` ctor bridge + `[W10-ENTRY]` diagnostic row (kills the `[REC-MISS]` ctor miss, gives regression visibility).

**E. Reproduction**
```
cd miniandroid && make -j2
rm -rf /tmp/tdata20 && mkdir -p /tmp/tdata20/out
timeout 190 ./build/miniandroid run --data-root /tmp/tdata20 -o /tmp/tdata20/out \
  --max-seconds 120 /tmp/my-project/apk_cache/termux_1022.apk
```
Post (measured, binary `56cf35bb4f4f3636`): `APUT-OBJECT store-check` rows **0** · `ArrayStoreException` rows **0** · `[W10-ENTRY]` ×8 (`ImmutableMap.entryOf` oids 79..109) · SYNTH-EXC **12, all caught/deferred (legal)** · boot advances to `TerminalView` onDraw + framebuffer 2073600/2073600 non-white px · exit=1 only for the KNOWN insets residual (below). Pre (wave-9 face): ASE ×17 uncaught.

**F. Integration** — header-only pure table additions: applies clean on any recent main, zero conflict surface. Unblocks every guava/collection-heavy app (ImmutableMap/RegularImmutableMap chains). Conflicts with nobody; enables W12 fragment work (VLC uses the same tables).

**Patch (complete):**
```diff
### va_W10-STORECHK (miniandroid/src/framework/view_ancestry.h)

@@ -438,6 +459,27 @@ framework_class_interfaces() {
         // app's own class_def declares none. The whitelist arm that accepts
         // enum values on ART is the same Serializable class.
         {"Ljava/lang/Enum;", {"Ljava/io/Serializable;", "Ljava/lang/Comparable;"}},
